Hi Kevin,

This customer we refunded US$72.00 / GBP49.49 last Thursday as part of 
RMA process. This customer has escalated this further to PayPal and 
Steve has asked if you will help and sort with PayPal.


Below is our step-by-step account of the issue reported to PayPal:


Customer:  Stephen Sidney ICN#51825            RMA#1209


- 20 Jan 2018:  customer makes an on-line order and PayPal payment for 
an ID#444, "Video to YCbCr / RGB Sync on Green Converter"


- Note: the customer selected and paid for the ID#444 through the 
products web-page without any contact to our Staff; the customer did not 
confirm any details about the product before or during the time of order


- 22 Jan 2018 order shipped to customer with his elected Courier, TNT


- 31 Jan 2018 customer emailed to say the product would not work with 
his applications; he indicated that at various times the converter did 
work with some of his applications, his issue was rolling TV picture


- after discussions over the following week, I suggested he needed a 
product that would also allow for NTSC/PAL conversion to overcome the 
problem, our ID#858 possibly


- 8 Feb 2018 customer advised to us the Courier and tracking details for 
the return of the product on RMA#1209. This RMA was issued to check 
condition of the product prior to any refund approval


- customer asked at this time if he was receiving full refund, including 
freight costs for all shipments. I referred him to the 'User Agreement' 
page on the Converters.TV website.


- Note:  All customers must accept the Terms and Conditions of the 
Agreement at the time of their order, so as to be able to proceed to 
make a payment for the order


- 15 Feb 2018 we received the ID#444  and it tested OK. Approval was 
given to refund the product cost only, as no freight or insurance is 
refundable as per 'User Agreement'


- 22 Feb 2018 customer emailed to say he had purchased another product, 
from another Company, that would work for his application. The product 
is a "Scart/S-Video to HDMI" converter


Please Note:  This HDMI product is a different video protocol compared 
to the product he ordered from us.

                          The customer when he ordered the ID#444, 
selected the incorrect product for his application


- 22 Feb 2018 customer was notified that he he had been refunded 
US$72.00 = GBP49.49 and to please confirm receipt of funds


- last communication


Please advise if any further information required.


Chris Bailey

Converters.TV





